'''Jewelled Crabs''' are found in the [[Chambers of Xeric/Strategies#Crab puzzle|crab puzzle]] room within the [[Chambers of Xeric]]. These crabs cannot be killed by conventional [[combat]]. However, the crystals which are on the crabs can be attacked in order to change their colour. Attacking with [[melee]] (or smashing it with a hammer) will cause a crab to change {{Colour|#ff0000|Red}}, [[magic]] for {{Colour|#0000ff|Blue}}, and [[ranged]] for {{Colour|#00ff00|Green}}.

They regenerate their stats at a rate of 1 per tick, faster than the standard rate of 1 per 100 ticks.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1524701424460628080|date=9 July 2026|quote=Stone guardians - 8 Muttadiles - 15 Vasa Nistirio - 10 Vasa's crystal - 9 Tekton - 15 LizardShamans - 20 Skeletal mystics - 25 Jewelled Crabs - 1 Vespula - 10 Vespula's portal - 45 Vespula's grubs - 10000 (i.e. never) Vespine soldier (flying) - 16 Vespine soldier (walking) - 10000 Otherwise default should be 100, as for outside CoX.|ctxquote=Hi@JagexAsh would you per chance be able to say the regen time (in ticks) for mobs in chambers?}}

For solo players, they can use a standard [[hammer]], or any [[blunt]] weapon with crush bonuses, including but not limited to: the [[dragon warhammer|(dragon)]] [[warhammer]](s), the [[elder maul]], the [[abyssal bludgeon]], the [[cursed goblin hammer]], [[Torag's hammers]], [[granite maul]], [[granite hammer]], [[frying pan]], [[meat tenderiser]], etc. and use the right-click "Smash" option on the crab. This will stun the crab in place for a while.

